CLASS:: EventScheduler
summary:: Plays a Klotho Score.write file with the semantics of Klotho's SuperSonic engine
categories:: Scheduling, External Control
related:: Classes/EventSchedulerGUI, Classes/KSPayload, Classes/KSAssets, Classes/KSMixer, Classes/KSTrace

DESCRIPTION::
EventScheduler loads the JSON file that Klotho's code::Score.write:: produces and plays it on a native scsynth exactly the way Klotho's browser engine (SuperSonic, code::scheduler_core.js:: and code::scheduler_score.js::) plays the same score:

list::
## code::defName:: on each event (code::synthName:: is accepted as a fallback); a missing name or code::sonic-pi-beep:: plays code::kl_tri::, code::__rest__:: plays nothing.
## Tracks from code::meta.groups::, each with a source group, an effects group and two buses; code::main:: last; code::"default":: and any unknown group name play on main, with one warning per unknown name.
## Insert chains from code::meta.inserts::, wired with code::inBus::/code::outBus::, intermediate buses as wide as the chain, and a bypass router on a track without inserts. A code::set:: event addressed to an insert's code::uid:: sets that node.
## Auto-release: an event with code::releaseAfter:: and a positive code::dur:: on a def that has a code::gate:: control gets code::/n_set gate 0:: at code::start + dur::. Gate presence is read from the compiled SynthDef through link::Classes/SynthDescLib::.
## Control envelopes from code::meta.controlEnvelopes:: and the companion code::<stem>.wav::: one control bus per descriptor preset with code::/c_set::, one code::__klEnvCtrl:: synth per descriptor at its start, code::/n_map:: on every target and pfield (deferred to code::startTime:: when later than the event). code::blockSize:: comes from code::meta.blockSize::, or is inferred as frames / descriptors.
## Spatial routing from code::meta.spatial::: width-N routers, main as wide as the widest array, code::out = srcBus + speakerLane::, and either the binaural fold (code::__spatialDecodeN:: with the geometry buffer) or the hardware array (code::__spatialArrayOutN::). Widths outside Klotho's precompiled family (1, 2, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32) are refused before any node exists.
## Finish at code::max(start + dur) + tailPause:: (code::onFinish::), the score group freed code::ringTime:: later, code::onIdle:: after that. code::stop:: frees only this player's score group: nothing else on the server is touched and no CmdPeriod runs.
## code::loop::: code::true:: or an integer number of cycles.
## Sample names on code::buf*:: pfields are loaded into buffers once per file and substituted at send time.
::

Every instant is sent as one time-tagged bundle (split by code::maxBundleBytes:: and code::maxBundleMsgs::, never inside one event's messages) code::latency:: seconds ahead, built as it goes. scsynth keeps at most 2048 time-tagged bundles per server and drops the next one silently, so an occupancy gate (link::Classes/KSQueueLoad::, the port of the browser engine's load tracker) keeps the bundles in flight under code::safeQueueLimit:: (1536) and waits for slots to come due before sending more: a flooded queue degrades to late delivery, never to lost notes. A gate release is never tagged within code::releaseGuard:: of its note's code::/s_new::, nor within code::lateReleaseGuard:: of the send of a note that went out late, because a code::gate 0:: applied before the voice's first calc leaves it hung.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: queueSlots
METHOD:: safeQueueLimit
METHOD:: minBatchBundles
METHOD:: maxBundlesPerSend
METHOD:: deferMin
METHOD:: deferMax
The occupancy gate, shared by every player: scsynth's queue size (2048), the working limit (1536), the headroom below which a send waits (25), the most bundles handed over between two checks (200) and the bounds of one wait (0.02 to 0.25 s).

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: server
The server to play on. Defaults to code::Server.default::.
ARGUMENT:: startupDelay
Seconds between code::play:: and the first event. Default 0.1, as in the browser.
ARGUMENT:: latency
How far ahead bundles are sent. Default code::server.latency::.
ARGUMENT:: ringTime
Seconds the score group stays alive after the piece ends. Default 5.
ARGUMENT:: enableMonitoring
Adds a level tap per track that sends code::/trackLevel:: (for the GUI's meters).
ARGUMENT:: debug
Posts debug lines.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: loadFile
Load a Score.write file in a Routine of its own; every refusal (unreadable file, a SynthDef the server does not have, a bad spatial width, a control buffer that does not divide into blocks) happens here. Also uploads the control-envelope buffer, the decoder geometry and the sample buffers.
ARGUMENT:: path
Path to the JSON file. The control buffer is read from the same path with a code::.wav:: extension.
ARGUMENT:: action
Called with code::(success, scheduler):: when the load is done.

METHOD:: loadFileSync
The same, from inside a Routine. Returns a Boolean.

METHOD:: loadSynthDefDir
Load every code::.scsyndef:: in a directory into the server and into link::Classes/SynthDescLib:: (so gate presence is known). Syncs when called inside a Routine.

METHOD:: loadKlothoDefs
Load Klotho's own bundled SynthDefs (code::assets/synthdefs/{infra,instruments,effects}::) from link::Classes/KSAssets#*klothoAssetsDir::.

METHOD:: play
Build the topology and start playback. Returns a Boolean. Playing while a previous play is live or ringing out frees that play first.

METHOD:: stop
Stop now. Frees this play's score group, buses and control buses, nothing else; fires no callback.

METHOD:: record
Record one pass of the loaded file to disk: the main output (N channels in code::\array:: mode, 2 in code::\fold::) to code::path::, plus one file per track when code::stems:: is true (code::<base>_<track>.<ext>::, at the track's width). Every file is opened before playback starts, so each one begins at the play's first instant. The output path may not be the file's own control-envelope code::.wav::.
ARGUMENT:: path
Output file.
ARGUMENT:: stems
Also write per-track files.
ARGUMENT:: onComplete
Called when the files are closed.

METHOD:: output
code::\array:: (hardware outputs 0..N-1), code::\fold:: (binaural decode onto outputs 0/1) or code::nil:: for automatic: code::\array:: when the server has at least N outputs. Changing it after a load reloads the file.

METHOD:: loop
code::false::, code::true:: (until stop) or an integer number of cycles.

METHOD:: ringTime
METHOD:: tailPause
METHOD:: latency
METHOD:: startupDelay
Timing parameters, in seconds.

METHOD:: stemTaps
When true, one stereo router per non-main track mirrors its post-fader bus onto hardware outputs 2+2i (the browser's stem capture layout).

METHOD:: onFinish
METHOD:: onIdle
METHOD:: onEvent
METHOD:: onLoad
Callbacks. code::onEvent:: receives the code::_stepIndex:: of each note that carries one.

METHOD:: oscTap
Sees every message the player sends: a link::Classes/KSTrace:: (which writes the parity trace format) or a Function code::{ |t, addr, args, sent, flags| }::. Lifecycle lines code::#defer [load, wait]:: and code::#releaseGuard [node, from, to]:: report a deferred send and a moved release.

METHOD:: maxBundleBytes
METHOD:: maxBundleMsgs
The most bytes (8192) and messages (250) in one bundle. An instant with more is split, between events.

METHOD:: releaseGuard
METHOD:: lateReleaseGuard
METHOD:: lateHorizon
The earliest a gate release may be tagged after its note's code::/s_new:: (0.003 s), and after the real send time of a note that went out late (0.05 s): a late bundle's node is not run before scsynth's next drain, and a code::gate 0:: applied before the first calc leaves the voice hung. code::lateHorizon:: (default 0) widens "late" to any send with less than that much lead; measured in isolation, a note and release sent together with under 25 ms of lead hang, but the stream only sends them together when it is catching up late.

METHOD:: lateSlotHold
How long (0.03 s) a bundle that was already due when sent is still counted in the queue: scsynth performs it at its next hardware callback, not on arrival.

METHOD:: deferCount
METHOD:: guardCount
METHOD:: queueLoad
How many sends the gate deferred and how many releases it moved in the current play, and the bundles the ledger currently counts in scsynth's queue.

METHOD:: allowUnknownDefs
When true, a def the SynthDescLib does not know is played anyway (treated as ungated) instead of refusing the file.

METHOD:: setTrackGain
METHOD:: muteTrack
METHOD:: soloTrack
Router gains for the GUI; they persist across plays.

METHOD:: trackNames
METHOD:: insertNames
METHOD:: status
METHOD:: payload
METHOD:: mixer
METHOD:: assets
Introspection.

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;
e = EventScheduler(s);
{ e.loadKlothoDefs; }.fork;          // Klotho's bundled defs, or e.loadSynthDefDir("path/to/compiled")
e.loadFile("piece.json", { |ok| if(ok) { e.play } });
e.stop;

// a 24-speaker file on a 24-output interface
e.output = \array;
e.loadFile("spatial_piece.json", { |ok| if(ok) { e.record("spatial_piece_render.wav", stems: true) } });

// trace every message in the parity format
t = KSTrace("trace.jsonl", (source: "native", firstPrivateAudioBus: s.options.firstPrivateBus));
e.oscTap = t;
e.onIdle = { t.write };
::

SECTION:: The file

code::{"meta": {...}, "events": [...]}:: as code::Score.write:: writes it. code::meta:: may carry code::groups::, code::inserts::, code::spatial::, code::controlEnvelopes::, and (from the native-player contract) code::blockSize::, code::defNames::, code::defs:: and code::samples::. Events carry code::type:: (new, set, release), code::id::, code::start::, code::defName::, code::dur::, code::releaseAfter::, code::pfields::, code::group::, code::speaker:: and code::speakerLane::. All times are seconds.
